-- title:
--   Trace and determinant agreement with the explicit octahedral lift
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group, let $F$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $\iota\colon\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]\to F$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $M\colon G\to M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ be a homomorphism into the multiplicative monoid of $2\times 2$ matrices, assumed to take all its values in the submonoid generated by the two explicit matrices [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Slift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L21) $=\begin{pmatrix}-1&1\\-1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Tlift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L23) $=\begin{pmatrix}1&-1\\-\sqrt{-2}&-1+\sqrt{-2}\end{pmatrix}$, and assumed to hit every element of that submonoid. Let $r\colon G\to M_2(F)$ be a homomorphism of multiplicative monoids all of whose values $r(g)$ are of finite order. Let $S\subseteq G$ be a set such that for every $\varphi\in S$ one has $\det r(\varphi)=\iota(\det M(\varphi))$ together with the alternative: either $\operatorname{tr} r(\varphi)=\iota(\operatorname{tr} M(\varphi))$, or else $\det M(\varphi)=1$, $\operatorname{tr} M(\varphi)=\pm 1$ and $\operatorname{tr} r(\varphi)=-2\,\iota(\operatorname{tr} M(\varphi))$. Assume further that every $\sigma\in G$ admits $\varphi\in S$, $g\in G$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$ with $r(\sigma)=r(g\varphi^{n}g^{-1})$ and $M(\sigma)=M(g\varphi^{n}g^{-1})$. Then for every $\sigma\in G$ both $\operatorname{tr} r(\sigma)=\iota(\operatorname{tr} M(\sigma))$ and $\det r(\sigma)=\iota(\det M(\sigma))$ hold.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic comparison step in the octahedral (Langlands–Tunnell) part of the argument: the submonoid generated by the two explicit matrices is the binary octahedral group of order $48$, and the hypothesis on $S$ allows, at the distinguished elements, the ambiguous "partner" trace value $-2\iota(\operatorname{tr} M(\varphi))$ attached to matrices of determinant $1$ and trace $\pm1$; the conclusion is that this ambiguity cannot in fact occur and that $r$ and the explicit lift $M$ have matching traces and determinants throughout $G$. It is used in [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_of_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_of_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair), where $G$ is a Galois group, $M$ the explicit lift of an octahedral residual representation and $S$ a set of Frobenius elements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift_trace_det_eq_of_agreeUpToPartner_of_conjPow.lean

